			<div class="content" id="post-content-4824116">
									

<p>As discussed on IRC this isn't very strong as a standalone piece, so I won't evaluate it as such, but I will want to evaluate its structure as a piece on progress.</p>
<p>An issue with this is that the fundamental stakes for the narrator/protagonist are not clear, except for that they have to wait a long time for a foregone conclusion. They clearly act during the time they are waiting, but their actions are actually glossed over and summarized. They don't appear to struggle to accomplish anything, even though they've accomplished a great amount of influence while they waited.</p>
<p>There was an opportunity here to create some amount of interesting nuance and contrast of simultaneously maintaining constant control and being completely out of control to act upon what has been gained, but I don't know if that was the intention of this piece. It was just something I noticed as a reader but the story didn't actually explore this.</p>

							</div>

