<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP 5127 was discovered in Chaco, Argentina in 2003 after civilians were consistently reporting deceased people rising from their graves.</p>
<p>SCP 5127 consists of SCP 5127-1 and SCP 5127-2. SCP 5127-1 is a strangely shaped book with covers made of an unknown harmful white substance and pages are made out of leather. The object appears to have the ability to resurrect deceased people.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -23 and three votes.</p>
<p>Feedback Ported:</p>
<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/iamwords2e" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5274191); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5274191&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605912172" alt="Iamwords2E" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5274191)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/iamwords2e" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5274191); return false;">Iamwords2E</a></span></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Format is confusing, you don't need to press enter every 2 lines that is just not how paragraphs work. Labeling of the instances is confusing, SCP-5127-2 and SCP-5127-3 could have their designations switched and it would flow better. Sentences are to simple and could be worded better so they are not as awkward. The SCP itself has little meat to and could use some plot (doesn't have to be a heavy one though) since at this point it is just the Necronomicon. You definitely have room for improvement but your asking for help is good sign. Though it is not recommended that you post articles on the main site of critique; The Wiki Sandbox in which drafts are posted for critique by designated wiki staff. Though I will warn you that it will likely be slow to hear a response though they are one of the better at giving critique that most other sources (even me). I hope this helps.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5136 is approximately 4 kilometers in length, 2 kilometers in width, and 100 meters in height, this anomaly is located in the Bahamas and is labeled “The Bahama Wonders Hotel”, the anomaly appears as a hotel, when the subject enters the Hotel they will be greeted by a man behind the desk, designated SCP-5136-1, he will be wearing formal attire. He will ask if the subject wishes to rent a room, if the subject says they are not they will be thrown out of the building from a strong force of wind, if the subject says they are looking for a room SCP-5136-2 will bring them to a random hallway, regardless if it is full or not, each hallway contains 40 doors leading to a room, these rooms are designated SCP-5136-2. For more information, read Addendum 1/332/CAI.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -24 and three votes.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5156 is a mutated virus that came from an unknown planet. It's appearance is a genderless Humanoid-shaped figure that has arms twirling uncontrollably every second for an odd reason. SCP-5156's capabilities are yet to be understood, but the one discovered is regeneration. SCP-5156's regeneration from wounds and such is absurd, it has come to a point where SCP-5156 can regenerate a limb for approximately 3 seconds. Sightings of SCP-5156 have been spotted in ██████. Thankfully, only a handful of people saw it. Further research of SCP-5156 is ordered by the 05 Council. Reports and Investigation will be available to those of Level 4+ Clearance.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -20 and three votes.</p>
<p>The supplementary pages SCP-5156 Investigation 001 and SCP-5156 Research Log 001 have likewise been deleted at -19 and -23 respectivley.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5234 resembles the nozzle of a common garden hose at its shortest length, but can expand and will most often be seen around 10 centimeters long. The &quot;hose&quot; will grow indefinitely, but its rate of growth differs depending on the environment. When any part of the &quot;hose&quot; is near plant life, SCP-5234 will rapidly elongate, and the longest recorded length has been one kilometer . SCP-5234 has been recorded to grow quicker around materials made of formerly organic material, such as wood, but it grows at its fastest rate when near live plants. SCP-5234 grows at its slowest when contained in a container of volcanic rock, with the most efficient type being obsidian.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -15 and three votes.</p>
<p>Feedback Ported:</p>
<p><span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/raitia" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4505266); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4505266&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605912172" alt="Raitia" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4505266)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/raitia" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4505266); return false;">Raitia</a></span></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>It's a creative concept for a non-agressive euclid, playing with the idea of a hose snake, that literally plays a game of snake with the enviroment, but it feels… underwhelming? The rust tidbit with rusting blood feels mostly like a danger for danger's sake addition, and beyond that it doesn't really do much more than slither around and grow. The containment procedures are also unnecessarily long and don't make sense. If It grows in organic material and destroys metal, why not just stick it in something like plastic?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5187 is a paperback book of the title The Whole Art of Deduction, however instances of SCP-5187 have been located with minor alterations to the title. Additionally, the author is credited variously under names associated with the fictional detective Sherlock Holmes. Efforts to trace the origins of these books have succeeded only in uncovering now-defunct publishing companies and publication dates for each book consistent with the final year of operation of each company.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -13 and three votes.</p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-5961 is an anomalous entity of unknown origin, although recovered documents suggest a Germanic origin. When observed SCP-5961 appears to be being of, what has been described as, ‘indescribable beauty’ by human beings observing it. This beauty is believed to overload dopamine production in the observer’s brain, creating an addiction to seeing and pleasing SCP-5961.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Deleted at -12 and three votes.</p>
<p>Rewrite by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bettermybutter" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2818841); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2818841&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1605912172" alt="BetterMyButter" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2818841)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/bettermybutter" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2818841); return false;">BetterMyButter</a></span> is pending.</p>
<hr />

