<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes<br />
<strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Weird</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> This creature resembles a demonic humanoid borne from human consciousness with a key anomaly embedded in its infectious presence. Anyone that either directly observes it or indirectly through secondhand description becomes convinced them to be a long-forgotten friend or lover they remember fondly, regardless whether said witnesses has any actual history with subject.<br />
Subject also possesses the ability to instantly teleport close by to anyone familiar with the entity’s existence, manifesting instantaneously around corners or behind doors. Whenever someone becomes informed about this creature, that person is immediately “marked” as a potential anchor destination for teleportation.<br />
Individuals who become more familiar with the subject heavily favors its opinion over even their closest peers, occupying their minds to near obsession. Individuals experiencing excess time spent in its presence become entirely occupied by thoughts of the entity, abandoning loved ones, and even disregarding basic needs like food or shelter in more extreme cases.<br />
The most notable and bizarre feature to this process, however, is that continued exposure to the demon’s anomalous presence is capable of erasing of any pre-existing mental manipulative affects placed upon any human’s psyche. Intervals of necessary exposure to the demon’s presence to perform this varies from days to years, depending on how powerful said previous manipulative alterations were. This property may indeed prove valuable to the foundation, though anyone proven to acknowledge devil's existence from both direct or indirect sources can only be remedied with large doses of Class A amnestic.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The demon was borne out of an unknown man’s own sacrifice to ritualistically create something from the collective unconscious of humanity. Subject finds mild entertainment in playing with the strings of the human mind it has such a great intuitive understanding about, preferring to use his powers to minimize aggression in his presence. It holds little empathy for humanity, though its indifference allows rare opportunities for it to cooperate with something that might grapple its attention; typically whatever may, in the subject’s words, “<em>make these mundane hours more interesting</em>.”</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The devil can be dangerous due to its powerful and evocative aura and teleportative capabilities, but it can also be utilized to counteract active influence mind-affecting SCP creatures.</p>
<p><strong>Tags:</strong> <em>compulsion, empathetic, humanoid, infohazard, mind-affecting, keter, sapient, sentient, teleportation</em></p>

